On Sat, 22 Jul 2006, azgor wrote:
>
> [2]: On April first, if you hallucinate on the plane of air (or maybe
> any plane), all of the monsters should appear to be snakes.

   Don't you mean "On August 18..."?

> [4]: Follow the Leader: when you have multiple pets and you climb
> stairs, not only should pets adjacent to you follow you but also pets
> adjacent to pets that are adjacent to you (etc.).

   I think the current behavior is a deliberate design decision to
make it hard to accumulate herds of pets. This would make the game
easier for pet-herders.

> [6]: You should be able to saddle any segment of a long worm. Pets
> should also be able to ride. With enough saddles, you and your Archon
> army can ride to battle on the same steed!

   Fun! The only problem is... long worms don't actually move, last
I checked. They just sit there and grow. I guess you could saddle
your long worm and wait for the battle to come to you...
   Also, if something out of sight kills your saddled long worm, and
its body disappears, do you suffer HP damage when you thump to the
floor?

> [9]: Give puddings a "critical mass".  When there are too many in one
> place, they go BOOM!!, creating holes, and tears in the fabric of
> space-time (magic portals and level teleporters).  Oh, and doing
> massive damage to any unfortunate who happens to be in the middle of it
> all....

   Silly, un-fun, and generally "huh?". However, if it weren't such a
pain to implement, I might like to see a patch in which a hallucinating
player could occasionally see a white unicorn and a black unicorn
collide, resulting in a magical explosion. :-/

> [11]: A "wait until fully healed or disturbed" command. Maybe if you do
> n1234. to wait a long time it stops waiting when you become fully
> healed. "You feel fully recovered. You stop waiting."

   This would be very useful. "1234" doesn't make sense, but the idea
would. It's been a very long time... doesn't Angband use '*' or '&'
for this purpose?

> [16]: CoMR: carrying a centaur corpse should grant magic resistance.
> GoP: carrying a gnome corpse should give a bonus to strength.  HoB:
> carrying a giant/minotaur/ettin/titan corpse should give a bonus to
> intelligence and wisdom.  WoW: invoking a blessed wraith corpse should
> have a chance of granting a wish (consuming the corpse in the process).

   I don't understand any of these. Are they just random suggestions
for alternatives to CoMR, GoP, etc.? If anything, lugging around a
giant corpse in the dungeon should give a massive /penalty/ to wisdom;
I mean, come on!

